# Secrets. .env was TRACKED and committed (4bcc94c) with no ignore rule —
# one `git add -A` away from pushing a service_role key, which bypasses every
# RLS policy in the database. Untracked in this commit; use .env.example.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Playwright's per-run output: screenshots and traces from the viewport sweep,
# plus its HTML report. Both are regenerated on every run and neither is a
# source artefact — the sweep's verdict is the exit code, not the folder.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Claude Code session transcripts exported into the repo. They are date-prefixed
# and can run to thousands of lines; one landed in ios/App/ and is not a source
# artefact. Ignored by shape rather than by name so the next one is too.
20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.txt

# Signing material, which is not source and must never reach the remote.
#
# An Apple .p8 turned up in the repo root on 2026-08-26, one `git add -A` away
# from being published. It had never been committed and nothing was stopping
# it. That key downloads from Apple EXACTLY ONCE and cannot be re-fetched, and
# a leaked one lets anybody mint Sign in with Apple client secrets for this
# team until it is revoked -- so the cost of the accident is not "rotate a
# password", it is "revoke the key, generate a new one, and re-sign".
#
# Keep the real thing outside the repo. scripts/apple-client-secret.mjs takes
# a path, so it never needs to live here.
*.p8
AuthKey_*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
ios/screenshots/

# Android signing. android/app/build.gradle reads the upload key's path and
# passwords from android/keystore.properties or from ANDROID_KEY* env vars; the
# properties file holds passwords in plain text and the keystore IS the key.
# Neither belongs in git. keystore.properties.example is the tracked template.
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
android/screenshots/

# Ruflo (claude-flow) is a local-only development harness. None of it is
# part of the product, and none of it is shared: the agent definitions, the
# hook handlers and the memory databases are all regenerated by `ruflo init`
# on whichever machine wants them. Committing them would put one developer's
# harness -- and the session state inside it -- in everyone else's checkout.
.claude-flow/
.swarm/
.agents/
ruvector.db
agentdb.rvf
agentdb.rvf.lock
.claude/agents/
.claude/commands/
.claude/helpers/
.claude/skills/
.claude/proven-config.json
.claude/.proven-config-version

# Per-machine Claude Code settings, which is where the Ruflo hooks live so
# that the tracked .claude/settings.json stays the shared one.
.claude/settings.local.json

# The Supabase CLI's own scratch directory. `cli-latest` is a version-check
# cache it rewrites on every invocation, so tracking it means every `supabase`
# command a developer runs shows up as a modified file. It was committed in
# #113 by accident rather than by decision.
supabase/.temp/

# Google Distance Matrix answers for the one-off routing referee; delete after.
scripts/routing-trials/.google-cache/
